+<body>
+<header><nav aria-label="Main navigation">
+<a class="brand" href="/"><img src="/icon-192.png" width="28" height="28" alt="">cells.garden</a>
+<a href="/guide/">Guide</a><a href="/chrome-extension/">Chrome</a><a href="/obsidian/">Obsidian</a><a href="/about/" aria-current="page">About</a>
+</nav></header>
+<main>
+<h1>Give your projects a place to grow</h1>
+<p class="lead">cells.garden is a project board and a pixel-art garden. Each project is a plant, and its cells hold your tasks, plans, ideas and progress.</p>
+<p>Use it on the web, in Chrome’s new tab, side panel or toolbar popup, and inside Obsidian. Start locally without an account, or sign in to sync and collaborate.</p>
+<p>Version 0.2.0 is our beta milestone across the three platforms. The garden is still growing: feedback and bug reports help shape what comes next.</p>
+<a class="button" href="/">Open your garden</a><a class="button" href="/guide/">Read the guide</a>
+<h2>Credits</h2>
+<p>Based on Max’s <strong>Garden Cells</strong>, whose garden design, pixel art and original Obsidian plugin made this project possible. The original is preserved in the <a href="https://github.com/lukketsvane/cells.garden/tree/original" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">source repository</a>.</p>
+<p>cells.garden is maintained by tastefinger and is free and open source under <a href="https://github.com/lukketsvane/cells.garden/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apache-2.0</a>.</p>
+<h2>Support the project</h2>
+<p>There are no paid features, ads or analytics. Supporting the project is optional and does not unlock extra features.</p>
+<p><a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/cells.garden" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Support cells.garden on Buy Me a Coffee</a></p>
+<h2>Questions and feedback</h2>
+<p><a href="https://github.com/lukketsvane/cells.garden/issues/new" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open a GitHub issue</a> or email <a href="mailto:cells.garden@proton.me">cells.garden@proton.me</a>. In the app, open the garden menu and choose <strong>Report issue</strong> for both options.</p>
+<p>Please keep passwords, sign-in links and private garden data out of public issues.</p>
+<h2>Your work stays yours</h2>
+<p>Work offline without an account. Optional sync stores your garden with the cells.garden service; shared members can see and edit what you share. Export a backup from the garden menu, and read the <a href="/privacy.html">privacy policy</a> for storage and account details.</p>
+</main>
+<footer><nav aria-label="Footer navigation"><a href="/">Open garden</a><a href="/privacy.html">Privacy</a><a href="https://github.com/lukketsvane/cells.garden">Source code</a></nav></footer>
+</body>
+</html>
